     <exercise>
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Study each context. For each context, find an equation. In each case, explain how you know your choices of slope and <m>y</m>-intercept are correct.
        </p>
      </introduction>
      <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Fia earns 3 points every time she finds a star in her <pubtitle>Dora the Explorer</pubtitle> game. She earns a one-time bonus of 50 points in each level for finding a banana for her monkey friend, Boots. Based on the number of stars she finds, how many points will Fia earn in a level if she always finds the banana?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Valen earns $5 each week for doing his chores. Each time his mom has to remind him, there is a $0.50 deduction from his allowance. How much will Valen earn in a week based on the number of times he needs to be reminded to do his chores?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

      <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            Jackson has $18. Each month, he pays $4 to stream music on his iPod. How much money does he have or owe based on the number of months he streams music?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

    </exercise>

</worksheet>